# THE SAME RESPONSE HEADERS, ON THE OTHER HOST.
#
# M2 fix wave 1 of the Cloudflare migration. Every rule below is a VERBATIM copy
# of a `[[headers]]` block in netlify.toml — same paths, same names, same values.
# `netlify/functions/lib/hosting.test.ts` parses both files and fails if one
# character drifts, because two of these three blocks are audit/bug fixes that
# were expensive to find and would be silent to lose:
#
#   /*                     the audit M-4 security set (frame-ancestors CSP)
#   /assets/*              L-1, immutable caching for content-hashed assets
#   /manifest.webmanifest  L-2, the manifest was served as application/octet-stream
#
# Vite copies public/ into dist/, and dist/ is what BOTH hosts publish. Netlify
# therefore also reads this file during the parallel run and merges it with
# netlify.toml. The values are identical by construction (the test enforces it),
# so the merge is a no-op in effect — but Netlify does not document its
# cross-source merge rule, so M3's first Netlify deploy after this change must
# `curl -I` /manifest.webmanifest and confirm ONE content-type, not two joined
# with a comma. See the M2 report, Fix wave 1.
#
# NOT APPLIED TO FUNCTION RESPONSES — on either host, identically:
#   Netlify:    "Custom headers apply only to files Netlify serves from our own
#                backing store. If you are proxying content to your site or
#                dealing with a URL handled by a function [...] custom headers
#                won't be applied to that content."
#   Cloudflare: "Custom headers defined in the _headers file are not applied to
#                responses generated by Pages Functions, even if the request URL
#                matches a rule defined in _headers."
# So /report and /api/* go unheadered on BOTH hosts today. That is pre-existing
# Netlify behaviour, not a migration regression, and closing it would make Pages
# diverge from Netlify mid-parallel-run. Booked as an M4 item instead.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/manifest.webmanifest
  Content-Type: application/manifest+json; charset=utf-8
